- id: quantum-fiber---working-with-salesforce-cases-qf-tech-assist_flow4
  name: What is a Salesforce Case?
  description: Cases are a powerful tool within Salesforce used for recording, tracking,
    and resolving issues. Cases facilitate interactions with customers, other agents,
    or teams to communicate and solve problems that might prevent an order from being
    assigned, such as facility or engineering issues. When a Quantum Fiber (QF) order
    cannot be completed due to company-related reasons requiring investigation, such
    as engineering or facilities issues, a Case is created to record, track, and resolve
    the problem. Additionally, automated cases may be generated based on specific
    error messages to address potential issues before the customer's due date, thereby
    preventing delays and avoiding unnecessary dispatches. Cases are managed through
    Salesforce queues and can be routed to various departments, enabling effective
    communication and collaboration to resolve problems. Salesforce Case Management
    supports the recording, tracking, and resolution of customer issues through sales,
    service, and support channels. This functionality includes capabilities to create
    cases from emails (email to case), web forms (web to case), manually, or via automation.
  steps: []
- id: quantum-fiber---working-with-salesforce-cases-qf-tech-assist_flow5
  name: Checklist
  description: ''
  steps: []
- id: quantum-fiber---working-with-salesforce-cases-qf-tech-assist_flow6
  name: Creating Cases in Salesforce
  description: 'TIP! Before creating a new case check to see if there is an existing
    case on the account that should be used. If so, update the Case Owner and Case
    Type instead of creating a new case. See Subject below. NOTE: Cases that have
    PDAP in the subject field should not be closed by QFTA. It is ok to modify the
    case, when appropriate (Tip: See the PDAP Cases section of this document.) Open
    a new case to account for the work or to send to another queue. If this Case Type
    is in the Facility Support queue, reassign it to the case creator. PDAP (Past
    Due Activation Project) is how Fiber Customer Success Team (FCST) tracks the past
    due and held orders to ensure it is followed up on and the customer is notified.
    To see the entire Case history for an Account, select Cases in the Highlight Panel
    (in the Related List Quick Links section)'
