    the FCST. This will not be used by QFTA.
  steps: []
- id: quantum-fiber---working-with-salesforce-cases-qf-tech-assist_flow8
  name: Reassign Case and Changing Ownership
  description: Once a case has been created, it can be reassigned to a different department
    by using the Reassign Case button. In the rare occasion that a Case needs to be
    reassigned to a person, see the Reassigning a Case to a Person section of this
    document. Open the case that changes need to be applied to and select Reassign
    Case.
  steps:
  - id: quantum-fiber---working-with-salesforce-cases-qf-tech-assist_step27
    question: Reassigning a Case to a Person
    options:
    - value: sasktel-service-order-assign-call-failure
      description: Sasktel Service Order Assign call failure
      solution: quantum-fiber---working-with-salesforce-cases-qf-tech-assist_sol1
    - value: the-process-failed-before-even-attempting-to-create-the-order-in-optius-therefor-this-is-not-a-valid-facility-support-case-and-the-case-should-be-reassigned-to-the-lpm
      description: The process failed before even attempting to create the order in
        Optius, therefor this is not a valid Facility Support case, and the Case should
        be reassigned to the LPM.
      solution: quantum-fiber---working-with-salesforce-cases-qf-tech-assist_sol2
    - value: sasktelunabletocomplete-30124---odin---unable-to-assign-resources-reason-me12487-rachael-dr-does-not-have-available-ports
      description: 'SASKTEL:UNABLE_TO_COMPLETE : 30124 - ODiN - Unable to assign resources,
        reason: ME=12487 RACHAEL DR does not have available ports'
      solution: quantum-fiber---working-with-salesforce-cases-qf-tech-assist_sol3
    - value: this-odin-error-will-still-be-valid-to-fallout-to-facility-support-however-this-happened-due-to-ows-and-subsequent-ciasn-order-pended-this-happened-before-the-aug-iia-tool-automation-will-resolve-new-instances-of-this-fallout-however-older-manual-fixes-will-be-required
      description: "This ODiN error will still be valid to fallout to Facility Support,\
        \ however this happened due to OWS and subsequent CIASN order pended.\_ This\
        \ happened before the Aug IIA tool automation will resolve NEW instances of\
        \ this fallout, however older manual fixes will be required"
      solution: quantum-fiber---working-with-salesforce-cases-qf-tech-assist_sol4
    - value: this-error-happened-because-the-ont-is-full-is-possible-in-other-scenarios-that-the-eng-design-needs-to-be-updated-if-more-addresses-were-assigned-to-the-ont-than-the-ont-is-capable-of-supporting-or-the-ont-size-may-need-to-be-changed-the-lpm-and-the-eng-will-work-together-to-resolve-the-issue-reassign-the-case-to-the-lpm
      description: This error happened because the ONT is full.  Is possible in other
        scenarios that the ENG design needs to be updated if more addresses were assigned
        to the ONT than the ONT is capable of supporting, or the ONT size may need
        to be changed. The LPM and the ENG will work together to resolve the issue.
        Reassign the case to the LPM.
      solution: quantum-fiber---working-with-salesforce-cases-qf-tech-assist_sol5
- id: quantum-fiber---working-with-salesforce-cases-qf-tech-assist_flow9
  name: Escalate
  description: The Escalate/Escalated buttons should not be selected by QFTA, unless
    following the Quantum Fiber - New Build Not Ready Escalation Process (QF Structure
    Load) process.  The NBNR process is the only time that QFTA should be escalating
    a case.
  steps: []
