  name: Related Documents
  description: ''
  steps: []
- id: 844g-integrated-ont-programming---calix-e7-cor-tsc-and-qf-tech-assist_flow4
  name: 844G ONT
  description: '844G is an integrated, all in one, ONT type that includes a built-in
    modem and ATA (analog telephone adapter). This ONT type uses the RG (residential
    gateway) port to program service, instead of the traditional GE port. When using
    the RG port, an ONT will incorporate all 4 GE ports, which means programming to
    the RG port will allow the technician to use ports 1, 2, 3 or 4 to get ping. If
    GE port 1 goes bad or does not ping, technicians can plug into port 2, 3 or 4
    and attempt ping without re-programming service. Special Notes on Programming:'
  steps: []
- id: 844g-integrated-ont-programming---calix-e7-cor-tsc-and-qf-tech-assist_flow5
  name: Switching from GE to RG Programming
  description: 'Important: to maintain database integrity, it is necessary to follow
    the steps below. Do not delete the ONT ID. Overview of Steps:'
  steps: []
- id: 844g-integrated-ont-programming---calix-e7-cor-tsc-and-qf-tech-assist_flow6
  name: Switching from RG to GE Programming
  description: 'Important: to maintain database integrity, it is necessary to follow
    the steps below. Do not delete the ONT ID. Overview of Steps:'
  steps: []
- id: 844g-integrated-ont-programming---calix-e7-cor-tsc-and-qf-tech-assist_flow7
  name: Auto-Switch Overview
  description: "An upgrade to CMS allows auto-switch of settings after an ONT is RONTA\u2019\
    d. Example: If an ONT is programmed as 700 series with GE services and an 844G\
    \ ONT is connected, CMS will automatically switch to 844G and move to RG-1 provisioning."
  steps: []
- id: 844g-integrated-ont-programming---calix-e7-cor-tsc-and-qf-tech-assist_flow8
  name: Changing ONT type from 844G to 803G or C5500XK
  description: "Previously 844G ONT\u2019s were only used for CTL-ON and Instant Internet\
    \ MDU Properties. If the technician needs to replace the 844G, whenever possible\
    \ it should be replaced with a different 844G. If that is not possible, recommend\
    \ that an 803G be used. A C5500KX maybe  used if the technician does not have\
    \ an 803G. Here are the steps to update the provisioning when changing from an\
    \ 844G to an 803G or C5500XK. Note: Do not delete the existing ONT."
  steps: []
- id: 844g-integrated-ont-programming---calix-e7-cor-tsc-and-qf-tech-assist_flow9
  name: Document Management
  description: ''
  steps: []
