- id: calix-e3-2-gpon-smx-programming-remote-tech-assist_flow4
  name: E3-2 GPON Overview
  description: 'E3-2 is an Intelligent PON Node that allows multiple PON technologies
    (GPON, XGS-PON and NG-PON2), and provides flexibility to fit various deployment
    configurations. E3-2 can support the same ONT card types as E7 GPON, including
    CASA DPU (ONT). Note: North Carolina field trial locations will be loaded into
    MARTENS and programmed Manually, while widescale deployments will be inventoried
    in O2 (Optius and ODiN) and supported by the Quantum Fiber stack, as well as programmed
    by OSG. Programming, troubleshooting and maintenance will be done through the
    SMx EMS.'
  steps: []
- id: calix-e3-2-gpon-smx-programming-remote-tech-assist_flow5
  name: Login
  description: 'The URL link to SMx has been updated. The previous URL, https://smx:3443  (also
    accessible via https://155.70.106.84:3443/smx/) and will no longer work at the
    start of the maintenance window. These URLs will be replaced by the new URL link
    provided in the Related Document section. This change will become effective on
    November 7, 2024. Important: Users are advised to utilize the new URL link instead
    of the IP address, if known. This allows the Element Management Systems (EMS)
    Support to effectively switch the application between Omaha and Denver servers
    without causing disruption to end-users, particularly during maintenance or when
    a data center is briefly unavailable. *Chrome is the preferred browser'
  steps: []
